  "name": "Question 17",
  "problem": "Simplify the statement $\u00ac(\u00acR\u21d2S).$",
  "worked_solution": "First, note that\n\n$$\n\u00ac(\u00acR\u21d2S)\u2261\u00ac(\u00ac(\u00acR)\u2228S).\n$$\n\nCanceling out double negations, we reach\n\n$$\n\u00ac(\u00ac(\u00acR)\u2228S)\u2261\u00ac(R\u2228S).\n$$\n\nFinally, we can distribute the negation over the disjunction using De Morgan's law:\n\n$$\n\u00ac(R\u2228S)\u2261\u00acR\u2227\u00acS\n$$\n\nSo the given statement is equivalent to $\u00acR\u2227\u00acS.$",
